book of neuropsychology</source><year>2000</year><edition>2nd</edition><publisher-name>Amsterdam, Elsevier</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Favart</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Coirier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acquisition of the Linearization Process in Text Composition in Third to Ninth Graders: Effects of Textual Superstructure and Macrostructural Organization</article-title><source>J Psycholinguist Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>305</fpage><lpage>328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16752086</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10936-006-9017-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garrod</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Saying what you mean in dialogue: A study in conceptual and semantic coordination</article-title><source>Cognition</source><year>1987</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>181</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3691025</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0010-0277(87)90018-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levelt</surname><given-names>WJM</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>S.Peters  and E.Saarinen </surname></name></person-group><article-title>Linearisation in describing spatial networks</article-title><source>Processes, beliefs and questions</source><year>1982</year><publisher-name>Dordrecht, Reidel</publisher-name><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>220</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schriefers</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lexical access in the production of noun phrases.</article-title><source>Cognition</source><year>1992</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1424498</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0010-0277(92)90022-A</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levelt</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>press MIT</surname></name></person-group><source>Speaking: from intention to articulation</source><year>1989</year><publisher-name>Cambridge, MA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>EV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the aqcuisition of the meaning of Before and After</article-title><source>Journal of verbal learning and verbal behavior</source><year>1971</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>266</fpage><lpage>275</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-5371(71)80054-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feagans</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Children's understanding of some temporal terms denoting order, duration, and simultaneity. </article-title><source>Journal of Psycholinguistic Research</source><year>1980</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7365706</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01067301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amidon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Carey</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why five-year-olds cannot understand Before and After.</article-title><source>Journal of verbal learning and verbal behavior</source><year>1972</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>417</fpage><lpage>423</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-5371(72)80022-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stevenson</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollitt</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The acquisition of temporal terms.</article-title><source>Journal of child language</source><year>1987</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>545</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3693459</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Partee</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Temporal and nominal anaphora</article-title><source>Linguistics and Philosophy</source><year>1984</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>286</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Natsopoulos</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Mentenopoulos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bostantzopoulou</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Katsarou</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Grouios</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Logothetis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding of relational time terms ''Before'' and ''After'' in Parkinsonian patients.</article-title><source>Brain Lang</source><year>1991</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>444</fpage><lpage>458</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1878778</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0093-934X(91)90142-N</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Natsopoulos</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grouios</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bostantzopoulou</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mentenopoulos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Katsarou</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Logothetis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Algorithmic and heuristic strategies in comprehension of complement clauses by patients with Parkinson's disease.</article-title><source>Neuropsychologia</source><year>1993</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>951</fpage><lpage>964</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8232851</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0028-3932(93)90150-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muente</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Schiltz</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kutas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>When temporal terms belie conceptual order</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1998</year><volume>395</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9738499</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/25731</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rodriguez-Fornells</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kutas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Muente</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Electrophysiological estimates of the time course of semantic and phonological encoding during listening and naming</article-title><so